    "pageContent": "1 BENTO/SLIDES The file is the software.One HTML file — deck, viewer and editor together. Open it anywhere. It saves itself.→ ADVANCE ESC EDIT S SPEAKER VIEW 2 02 ONE FILE 02 Everything ships inside. your deck — JSON in a <script> block viewer + presenter — morphs, charts, speaker view the editor itself — press Esc, it’s right there Self-saving — ⌘S rewrites this very file in place No install, no account — a browser is the whole runtime Assets embedded — images and fonts ride along as data View-source honest — your document is readable JSON Updates? The file checks a signed manifest at launch — you can turn that off — and rewrites itself.5 04 NO MOVING PARTS Software with nothing to install, break, or expire.1 0 100% FILE TO SEND SERVERS REQUIRED YOURS, FOREVER 6 LIVE DATA 06 Charts with a pulse. 0 20 40 60 80 100 Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Views Edits Hover the bars — tooltips are live. Scroll or pinch inside the chart to zoom the data.See the split → pie split LIVE DATA 06 Same chart. New shape. Mon 13% Tue 21.1% Wed 16.7% Thu 26.6% Fri 22.6% Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri This is a hidden state — arrow keys skip it; only the click gets here. The data morphed in place.See the spread → scatter LIVE DATA 06 And a scatter, in place. 0 10 20 30 40 50 60 70 80 Engagement 0 20 40 60 80 100 Owned Paid Same chart element — a third form. Each dot is a campaign: reach across, engagement up.↺ Back to bars 8 STORY WITH DATA 08 Momentum you can feel.+975% 0 20 40 60 80 100 Jan Feb Mar Apr May Jun Jul Aug Sep Oct Nov Dec 9 09 MOTION 09 Lines that lead the eye. DRAFTED REVIEWED SHIPPED Drawn with the on-canvas path editor — drag the anchors and the loop follows.10 INTERACTIVE STATES 10 One cast. Three scenes.01 a tidy grid Play scene 2 → Every scene is an ordinary slide — arrange elements, link a button, done.scene 02 INTERACTIVE STATES 10 One cast. Three scenes.02 a loose cascade Play scene 3 → Every scene is an ordinary slide — arrange elements, link a button, done.scene 03 